concepts.body:
The `maven-publish` plugin uploads a project's artifacts to any repository that works like Maven's: Maven Central (through Sonatype, the company that runs it), a company server such as Nexus or Artifactory, GitHub Packages, or `mavenLocal()` (the `~/.m2` folder on your own computer) for testing.

Configure a **publication**, a set of files to publish together, from the `java` component (what the `java` plugin builds) and one or more **repositories**:

```kotlin
publishing {
    publications { create<MavenPublication>("maven") { from(components["java"]) } }
    repositories { maven { url = uri("https://nexus.acme.com/repository/maven-releases") ; credentials { ... } } }
}
```

This generates tasks like `publishMavenPublicationToMavenRepository` and the aggregate `publish`, plus `publishToMavenLocal`.

The component turns Gradle's `api` dependencies into Maven's `compile` scope and `implementation` into `runtime`, so projects built with Maven get a sensible **POM**, the XML file that describes a published library and its dependencies. Gradle also publishes a `.module` file with richer **metadata** (variants and capabilities, see the Expert lessons) that Gradle users read.

Add `java { withSourcesJar(); withJavadocJar() }` to publish JARs of the source code and of Javadoc (documentation generated from code comments), which Maven Central requires, together with POM details (name, description, website, license, developers, source repository) set through `pom { }`. The `signing` plugin adds a **digital signature** made with GPG, an encryption tool, proving the files came from you; Central requires that too.

Use `group` and `version` for the coordinates; Versions ending in `-SNAPSHOT` mark work in progress: they go to separate snapshot repositories and may be published again under the same number. Never put **credentials** (user names, passwords, tokens) in the script: read them from `gradle.properties` in your **home directory** or from **environment variables** (`providers.environmentVariable("NEXUS_TOKEN")`).

concepts.code:
plugins { `java-library`; `maven-publish`; signing }
group = "com.acme"
version = "1.2.0"
java { withSourcesJar(); withJavadocJar() }
publishing {
    publications {
        create<MavenPublication>("maven") {
            from(components["java"])
            pom {
                name = "acme-core"
                description = "Core utilities for ACME services"
                url = "https://github.com/acme/core"
                licenses { license { name = "Apache-2.0" } }
                developers { developer { id = "ada"; name = "Ada L." } }
                scm { url = "https://github.com/acme/core" }
            }
        }
    }
    repositories {
        maven {
            name = "nexus"
            url = uri("https://nexus.acme.com/repository/maven-releases")
            credentials(PasswordCredentials::class)   // nexusUsername / nexusPassword properties
        }
    }
}
signing { useGpgCmd(); sign(publishing.publications["maven"]) }
// $ ./gradlew publishToMavenLocal      $ ./gradlew publish

// build-logic/src/main/kotlin/com/acme/GreetingPlugin.kt
package com.acme

import org.gradle.api.*
import org.gradle.api.file.RegularFileProperty
import org.gradle.api.provider.Property
import org.gradle.api.tasks.*

abstract class GreetingExtension { abstract val message: Property<String> }

@CacheableTask
abstract class GreetTask : DefaultTask() {
    @get:Input abstract val message: Property<String>
    @get:OutputFile abstract val output: RegularFileProperty
    @TaskAction fun run() = output.get().asFile.writeText(message.get())
}
class GreetingPlugin : Plugin<Project> {
    override fun apply(project: Project) {
        val ext = project.extensions.create("greeting", GreetingExtension::class.java)
        ext.message.convention("Hello")                       // default, overridable
        project.tasks.register("greet", GreetTask::class.java) {
            it.message.set(ext.message.map { m -> "$m from ${project.name}" })   // lazy wiring
            it.output.set(project.layout.buildDirectory.file("greeting.txt"))
        }
    }
}
// consumer build.gradle.kts:  plugins { id("com.acme.greeting") }   greeting { message = "Hi" }
// $ ./gradlew greet && cat build/greeting.txt   -> Hi from app

